{"study_accession":"PRJNA629540","secondary_study_accession":"SRP259336","title":"Radiation-induced bystander effect impaired human hematopoietic stem cells by oxidative DNA damage","description":"With the immunodeficient mouse model coupled with TBI and coculture system, we found that the radiation-induced bystander effect also occurred to human hematopoietic cells. The long-term hematopoietic reconstitution of bystander human HSCs was significantly decreased, and the colony-forming ability of bystander human hematopoietic progenitor cells was reduced. Further study found that the bystander human hematopoietic cells initiated enhanced DNA damage responses (DDRs), cell cycle arrest and p53-dependent apoptosis, mainly due to oxidative stress. Moreover, some antioxidants could mitigate this bystander effect with different efficacies both in vitro and in vivo. Overall design: Human CB-CD34+ cells were cocultured with 10 Gy IR or NR human BM cells using a transwell system. After 17 hours of coculture, the CD34+ cells in the insert were collected for RNA-seq.","pubmed":"33881475","geo_series":"","n_samples":10,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN14779621","study_accession":"PRJNA629540","blood_class":"cord_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"NR_5","description":"NR_5","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM4506623","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-03-30","attributes":[["source_name","cord blood"],["tissue","cord blood"],["cell_type","CD34+ cells"],["co-cultured with","NR human BM"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR11653414","experiment_accession":"SRX8214453","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"HiSeq X Ten","read_count":28808629,"base_count":8642588700,"first_public":"2021-03-30","experiment_title":"HiSeq X Ten sequencing: GSM4506623: NR_5 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN14779622","study_accession":"PRJNA629540","blood_class":"cord_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"IR_5","description":"IR_